{
  "_comment": "📏️ Window measures on wgpu: `section` is the canonical JSON the guest publishes on the reserved `framework.section.measures` retained surface (per window instance). `windows[].expectedOverlay` is the ui_contract document the wgpu Shell projects into that window's Measures overlay (general measures only — a group tagged `activeUtilityId` belongs to the Utility Options rail; `progress` is not a measure here). Components and bindings are the contract wire JSON. `gestures` are operated on the painted overlay and must dispatch the measure's `onChange` with React's payload and the owning window instance.",
  "surfaceBodyKey": "framework.section.measures",
  "section": {
    "puzzle3d-main": [
      {
        "kind": "number",
        "id": "puzzle3d-fill-count",
